+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U9","attempt":2,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/U9/verdicts/A1-reviewer.json R1, R2, R5; docs/trace/ui/U9/verdicts/A1-security.json S1","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"U9-acceptance-4/5/8","layer":"tests","files":["infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml","infrastructure/pipelines/check-pipeline.py"],"root_cause":"Symptom: Deploy_<env> ships only the App Service zip. Cause: the attempt-1 builder stopped at its 25-minute box (gate.write detail in docs/trace/ui/U9/packet/gates.jsonl:1: 'Builder stopped at its 25m box after committing 7910201, 8f23c27') before writing the web deploy. The deploy steps at infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml:73-160 are infra (75-97), migrations (116-125), DB grant (130-141), az webapp deploy (143-154) and the /health/ready curl (156-160). No step reads the Static Web App deployment token from the resource, deploys the `web` artifact (published at infrastructure/pipelines/azure-pipelines.yml:122-124) with the SWA CLI, or smoke-tests the site root. Acceptance line 8 asks for the web build 'before the Static Web Apps deploy', line 4 for 'a web build and deploy stage', and line 5 for 'deployment token from the resource, never in params'. The check passed anyway because infrastructure/pipelines/check-pipeline.py has no assertion on the deploy job for a Static Web App deploy, a token read or a site smoke test (the Web-stage needles at 52-53 cover only the build side). That is the reviewer's R6, already deferred. Not verified here: deployment jobs auto-download the current pipeline's artifacts, as the job already uses `drop` at stage-template.yml:68-69 without a download step, so the missing piece is the deploy, token and smoke steps, not necessarily a download step. Fix direction: in the deploy job, after the app deploy, add a step on the ARM connection that reads the token from the site named by $(webSiteName) into a masked secret variable, a step that deploys $(Pipeline.Workspace)/web with a pinned SWA CLI with the token passed through the step's environment (never a parameter or variable group), and a curl --fail of https://$(webHostName)/. Constraints: check-pipeline.py:120-121 requires the last step to curl /health/ready, so either the site smoke test joins that last step or that assertion is widened (in scope). The pipeline.schema.json task branch (136-144, additionalProperties false) has no `env`, so a task step carrying the token needs that branch widened, or the token must go through a script step, whose branch already allows `env` (118).","fingerprint":"U9-acceptance-4/5/8|infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml|swa-deploy-steps-missing","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml as at HEAD, When python -I infrastructure/pipelines/check-pipeline.py runs with new assertions that the deployment job has a step running 'az staticwebapp secrets list' that emits a secret (issecret=true) variable, a step that deploys the 'web' artifact path with a version-pinned SWA CLI taking the token only through env, and a curl --fail of https://$(webHostName)/, Then it exits 1 at HEAD and 0 once the steps exist (check-pipeline.py, the pipeline schema check)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"code-quality","layer":"tests","files":["infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml","infrastructure/pipelines/check-pipeline.py","infrastructure/pipelines/pipeline.schema.json"],"root_cause":"Same cause as I1 (R1): this is what the unfinished SWA deploy left behind. Symptom: stage-template.yml:90-91 sets webSiteName and webHostName, and nothing reads $(webSiteName) or $(webHostName). The new `env` property on the script-step branch at pipeline.schema.json:118 is used by no step (no 'env:' in either pipeline YAML). Why the dead variables passed: the I3 'no dead outputs' assertion at check-pipeline.py:169-170 counts a main.bicep output (main.bicep:113-114) as consumed if the string '.<output>.value' appears in the template. The jq setvariable line meets that by itself, so the output looks consumed when no step uses it. Fix direction: fixing I1 gives the two variables and the schema `env` branch real readers. Separately, tighten the I3 consumption check to require that the variable set from each output is referenced as $(<name>) by a later step, so a set-but-unread variable fails.","fingerprint":"code-quality|infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml|swa-outputs-set-never-read","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given stage-template.yml sets webSiteName and webHostName via setvariable and no step references $(webSiteName) or $(webHostName), When check-pipeline.py runs with the I3 assertion requiring each setvariable'd main.bicep output to be read as $(<name>) by a later step, Then it fails naming webSiteName and webHostName, and passes once the I1 steps read them (check-pipeline.py, the pipeline schema check)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"U9-acceptance-9","layer":"tests","files":["infrastructure/README.md"],"root_cause":"Same cause as I1 (R1): the README was written for the full design, and the time box cut the pipeline off before it matched. Symptom: infrastructure/README.md:72 says Deploy 'deploys the web artifact to the Static Web App, and smoke-tests the site', 83-85 describe the token read via 'az staticwebapp secrets list' into a masked variable for a pinned SWA CLI, and 89 says Deploy_<env> deploys the artifact and smoke-tests the site root. None of these steps exist at stage-template.yml:73-160. README:90-91 says 'the token step and the CLI deploy are schema-checked and read by eye', which is false for steps that don't exist. Acceptance line 9 asks the README to document the Static Web App and the web stage 'in the style of its App Service sections', which describe steps that are in the files. The README describes intent, not files. Fix direction: once I1 is built, re-read README lines 72 and 80-94 against the steps line by line, so every step named exists in the template with the names and pinning stated. If any step is dropped, remove its sentence rather than keep a claim.","fingerprint":"U9-acceptance-9|infrastructure/README.md|readme-describes-absent-swa-steps","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"No harness reads infrastructure/README.md. check-pipeline.py parses only the two YAML files, the schema and the Bicep (check-pipeline.py:32-35, 128-136), and the doc check renders the trail, not this README. An assertion that README sentences match YAML steps would test wording, not behaviour. The behaviour behind the claims is covered by I1's checker test, and the prose match is checked by the reviewer's re-read."},{"id":"I4","rule_id":"API8:2023","layer":"tests","files":["infrastructure/README.md","infrastructure/pipelines/stage-template.yml"],"root_cause":"Same cause as I3 and I1 (security S1 is the same drift that R2 reports). Symptom: infrastructure/README.md:83-85 claims the deployment token is read from the resource at deploy time, held in a masked variable and passed to the CLI through an environment variable. stage-template.yml has no such step (its only diff is the two setvariable lines at 90-91), so the no-secret claim describes handling that doesn't exist and can't be verified. No token, key or credential is in the diff. The secret-literal scan at check-pipeline.py:126-127 still passes, but there is no token handling for it to scan. Fix direction: the I1 token step is what makes the claim true. It must read the token at run time, mark it secret, pass it to the CLI only through the step's environment, and never echo it or put it in a parameter, variable group or bicepparam. The README then describes that step exactly.","fingerprint":"API8:2023|infrastructure/README.md|token-handling-claimed-not-built","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"The finding is about a README claim, and no harness reads infrastructure/README.md (check-pipeline.py:32-35 loads only the YAML, the schema and the Bicep). Once the token step exists, its secret handling becomes checkable through I1's assertion (issecret=true and passed only through env), and the existing literal scan at check-pipeline.py:126-127 covers values in the YAML. Neither of those reads the README text."}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1 · t1 write by the builder, stopped at its 25-minute box after 7910201 and 8f23c27 · gate.write ok · scoped gates ok · reviewer FAIL A1 (P0 R1, P1 R2, P0 R3, P1 R4, P2 R5-R7), security PASS A1 (P2 S1, S2). First investigation on U9, so no fingerprint recurs. The attempt-1 cause was the time box cutting off unfinished work, not a wrong fix, so attempt 2 should finish the SWA deploy steps and then align the README."]}
