+---
+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U9","attempt":2,"source":"david","source_ref":"steer(D2,pause2) in docs/trace/ui/U9/loop.jsonl:57 (head 1d637b3); gate.qa-run Part A exit 1 at loop.jsonl:58","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"U9-acceptance-6","layer":"tests","files":["Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch","src/web/.vscode/launch.json","src/web/Docket.Web.esproj"],"root_cause":"Symptom: F5 with the 'API and web' profile starts the API, then opens an Edge window on http://localhost:4170 that cannot connect. Cause: in a multi-project launch profile, Visual Studio runs the .esproj's DebugTarget instead of its StartupCommand, and the target D1 chose only opens a browser. Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch:13 names DebugTarget 'localhost (Edge)'. src/web/.vscode/launch.json:5-9 defines it as type edge, request launch, url http://localhost:4170, with nothing that starts a server. The StartupCommand at src/web/Docket.Web.esproj:4 ('npx vite --port 4170 --strictPort') is never run on this path, so nothing listens on 4170. The comment at Docket.Web.esproj:3 ('F5 runs the Vite dev server') is false for this profile. Evidence: David's experiment (loop.jsonl:57). He changed the StartupCommand to 'cmd /k npx vite ...', and F5 opened only the API console, with no second console. 'Start New Instance' on Docket.Web alone does run the StartupCommand, so the earlier F5 pass (signoff 62525a5, loop.jsonl:53) was served by a Vite left running from that. David's fix was verified on his machine: a node-type launch configuration 'Vite dev server' (program node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js, args --port 4170 --strictPort --open) named as the DebugTarget. Recurrence: not the same cause as D1/I2, so this gets a new fingerprint. It is the same rule and the same files, and it comes from D1's own fix direction. D1/I2 correctly found that DebugTarget was missing, which caused the 'previously selected debugger' popup. It then directed a browser-type target on the assumption that the StartupCommand also runs, and flagged that assumption as unprovable from the repo (docs/trace/ui/U9/findings/D1.md:14, I2 'Uncertainty, stated honestly'). That direction fixed the popup and left the dev server unstarted. Why D1 and A2.2 missed it: D1 assumed the SDK's React-template convention without a run. The A2.2 reviewer said in its verdict that the files don't prove the SDK starts Vite and deferred to David's F5 (docs/trace/ui/U9/verdicts/A2.2-reviewer.json:84). The one F5 that followed passed only because a stale Vite was still running (loop.jsonl:53 vs :57). The only test checks file shape, so it pinned the assumption rather than testing it (I2). This finding and I2 share one cause and are kept as two findings on purpose: I1 is the launch configuration, I2 is the test that pins it. Fix direction: deferred to U10 by David, and U9 gets no fix round. Docket.Web's DebugTarget in the profile must name a launch configuration that runs Vite itself, on the StartupCommand's port. The Edge configuration stays for Start New Instance. Correct the esproj comment. This is U10's 'One-key F5' acceptance line (docs/plans/active/ui.dag.yaml:591).","fingerprint":"U9-acceptance-6|Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch|debug-target-replaces-startupcommand-browser-only","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch, src/web/.vscode/launch.json and src/web/Docket.Web.esproj, When the test resolves the 'API and web' profile's Docket.Web entry DebugTarget to exactly one launch.json configuration, Then that configuration is request 'launch' of type node whose program is node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js and whose args carry --port equal to the StartupCommand's --port (4170) and --strictPort. It fails at HEAD, where the target is 'localhost (Edge)', type edge, with no program. That Vite actually comes up on F5 stays David's HITL check, because no test can drive Visual Studio's launcher (LaunchProfileTests in Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"U9-acceptance-6","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests/LaunchProfileTests.cs"],"root_cause":"Same cause as I1: this is the test that pins I1's wrong target, and it is now known to be wrong. The two are kept as separate findings on purpose. API_and_web_profile_debugs_the_web_app_in_one_browser_launch_configuration_on_the_dev_server_port (LaunchProfileTests.cs:71-86) requires the Docket.Web DebugTarget to be a browser configuration. Line 84 asserts type is 'edge' or 'chrome', and line 85 asserts a url of http://localhost:{port}. The comment at :69-70 states the premise that turned out false: 'The JavaScript SDK's F5 targets are the browser configurations'. The test passes at HEAD on a profile that cannot serve the web app, and David's verified fix (a node target with no url) would fail it. It was written red-first from D1/I2's suggested test (D1.md:14), which carried D1's unverified assumption into an assertion. Fix direction: at U10, the test is changed red first to require a DebugTarget that runs Vite on the StartupCommand's port, as U10's line says (ui.dag.yaml:591). The other launch tests (:18-67) are unaffected.","fingerprint":"U9-acceptance-6|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests/LaunchProfileTests.cs|asserts-browser-debug-target","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the same three files, When the reworked test reads the Docket.Web DebugTarget configuration, Then it asserts type node, the Vite program and the StartupCommand's port, and no longer accepts an edge or chrome type without a server. Written red against HEAD's 'localhost (Edge)' target, before the slnLaunch and launch.json change (LaunchProfileTests in Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"U9-acceptance-10","layer":"tests","files":["README.md","docs/qa/ui-U9.md"],"root_cause":"Same cause as I1. The F5 prose describes what the D1 design was assumed to do, not what Visual Studio does. README.md:17-19 says F5 starts 'the web dev server on http://localhost:4170, with an Edge debug window on that address'. On F5 the dev server never starts, and the Edge window cannot connect. README.md:150-151 points to the same profile. The QA script repeats this. docs/qa/ui-U9.md:53 (step 4) expects Docket.Web's target to be 'localhost (Edge)'. Step 5 at :54 expects 'A second console runs npx vite --port 4170 --strictPort ... and a debug browser (Edge) opens the web app'. Steps 6-7 at :55-56 build on that. :8 and :121 say F5 uses the dev server on 4170. With David's fix, the browser is the default one opened by Vite's --open, not a VS-attached Edge window, so the wording changes too. This is not a recurrence of D1/I3, which was about the unread profile file name; that part is now correct (README.md:17, ui-U9.md:7). Why it was missed: D1/I3's direction said to re-read the README against an actual F5 (D1.md:14), and the A2.2 reviewer checked it against the files instead (A2.2-reviewer.json:82). The only F5 run was masked by the stale Vite. Fix direction: at U10, per its line (ui.dag.yaml:591), README.md and docs/qa/ui-U9.md say what F5 opens: the API with its /health/live tab, and Vite started by the 'Vite dev server' target, which opens the default browser on 4170. QA step 4 names the new target. The sign-off at loop.jsonl:59 already records that these two files overstate F5.","fingerprint":"U9-acceptance-10|README.md|f5-wording-claims-vite-and-edge-debug-window","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"No test project or gate reads README.md or docs/qa/ui-U9.md. This follows the D1/I3 and A1 precedent: render-trace reads the QA table's rule column, not its expectations. A test of these sentences would test wording, not behaviour. The behaviour they describe is pinned by I1's test, and the prose match is David's F5 at U10's pause."}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1 · reviewer FAIL A1 (SWA deploy steps, dead outputs, README describes absent steps) · security PASS A1 · investigator A1 fingerprints swa-deploy-steps-missing, swa-outputs-set-never-read, readme-describes-absent-swa-steps, token-handling-claimed-not-built","attempt 2 · D1 from David: slnlaunch-named-with-slnx-extension, esproj-no-browser-debug-target, f5-steps-name-unread-profile-file, avast-detection-unidentified · fixed and passed as A2.2 at ca43c93 · signoff 62525a5 on an F5 that a stale Vite had served","attempt 2 · D2 from David at 1d637b3: no new fingerprint repeats a D1 one, but I1 and I2 come from D1/I2's fix direction (a browser target, assuming the StartupCommand still runs). That fixed the debugger popup, not the serving. David moved the fix to U10 (ui.dag.yaml:591), and U9 was re-signed at 1d637b3 with the gap recorded (loop.jsonl:59)."]}
